From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: give a BSS the RUID of its radio

The bss table is permanently empty on hardware. Every agent reports its BSSes correctly -
a capture of the AP Operational BSS TLV (0x83) shows fourteen of them across
three nodes, with BSSIDs and SSIDs - and the controller parses them into
r->iflist, so mapc_sync_bss() does run once per BSS.

It just cannot write them:

    bss.ruid TEXT REFERENCES radio(ruid)

mapc_sync_bss() binds b->ruid, but nothing on the Topology Response path ever
fills that field in. cntlr_radio_add_iface() has the radio in hand and sets
is_fbss, is_bbss and enabled, yet leaves bss->ruid zeroed; the only two writers
of a BSS ruid in the controller sit in an unrelated TLV handler. So every insert
carries ruid "00:00:00:00:00:00", matches no radio row, and is rejected.

Measured on 2026-07-21: an agent reporting two BSSes produced exactly two
"FOREIGN KEY constraint failed" entries, one reporting six produced exactly six.

Copy the RUID from the radio the interface is being attached to, on both the
newly allocated and the already existing path. radio.ruid and
operating_class.ruid are both written from r->radio_el->macaddr, so this uses
the same identity and the key matches.

--- a/src/cntlr.c	2026-07-21 11:57:02.472981611 +0200
+++ b/src/cntlr.c	2026-07-21 11:57:04.022196131 +0200
@@ -879,6 +879,10 @@
 	if (n) {
 		n->bss->enabled = true;
 		n->radio = r;
+		/* The BSS carries the RUID of the radio it belongs to; without it
+		 * mapc_sync_bss() writes an all-zero ruid and the bss row is
+		 * rejected by the foreign key into radio(ruid). */
+		memcpy(n->bss->ruid, r->radio_el->macaddr, 6);
 		return n;
 	}
 
@@ -910,6 +914,7 @@
 	n->bss->is_fbss = true;
 	n->bss->is_bbss = false;
 	n->bss->enabled = true;
+	memcpy(n->bss->ruid, r->radio_el->macaddr, 6);
 	list_add(&n->list, &r->iflist);
 	n->agent = r->agent;
 	n->radio = r;
